cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Code and data for: Print the trivial arm, then print the other metric: a fidelity-perception reversal and an initialisation-dependent stall in an image restoration comparison
message: If you use this code or data, please cite this archive and the manuscript.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Zeyu
    family-names: Fu
    email: fuzeyu99@126.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0001-8329-0108'
    affiliation: 'Army Medical University, Chongqing, China'
abstract: >-
  Toy training records and a nine-cell initialisation ablation, per-crop PSNR/SSIM and LPIPS-AlexNet tables for a released restoration model and two interpolations on the published RealSR crop128 protocol, camera-stratified metrics, inference manifests, a memory-ceiling skip census, predeclarations and receipts, figure code and manuscript source for an estimand and baseline audit across three scales. The crop128 protocol is the published test split; the census (206/193/13) is hardware-selected and reported separately.
keywords:
  - image restoration
  - super-resolution
  - baselines
  - perception-distortion tradeoff
  - evaluation
  - selection effect
  - negative result
